## New Capabilities Identified

- **Onboarding surface set** — hero/tagline row, "start anywhere" side-panel empty state with folder + status legends and starting-point suggestions, stats footer (`N nodes · M connections · built from K sources` + "Esc to reset" hint).
- **Rich, browsable detail panel** — colored folder badge, per-page description (frontmatter `description:` with first-body-paragraph fallback, emitted by `build-graph` into `graph-data.json`), connected pages grouped by folder as clickable chips that select the target node.
- **Search everywhere** — semantic search wired to swim-lane mode (fixes A1), promoted to an always-visible header slot with a result count and Ctrl+K / `/` focus affordance.
- **Keyboard support** — Esc de-escalation chain (tour → popover → search → selection); footer hint matches behavior (fixes A4).
- **Responsive layout** — 390px floor; side panel as bottom sheet/overlay on small viewports (fixes A5).
- **Visual identity pass** — Geist fonts actually applied (fixes A9), deliberate surface palette + folder-accent system, full-text pill labels (B5), tinted descriptor-labeled lane containers (B6), hover/focus states, type hierarchy (B10).
- **Guided tour** — single hand-curated "Take a tour" path through 4–5 linked nodes with captions and progress indicator, driven by a static tour definition.
- **Force-directed demo-worthiness** — camera re-fit on layout switch + reset-view control (A2); centered click-zoom landing with selection ring, connection highlighting, dimming, theme-aware link colors, label decluttering (A6).
- **Swim-lane transparency** — "+N more" affordance for zero/low-degree nodes instead of silent dropping (A7); explainer copy corrected to match per-mode UI (A8).
- **Working source links** — path-join fix in `lib/github-source-link.ts` + repo made public after a git-history privacy audit (A3).
- **Demo-vault research ingestion (dedicated epic)** — author supplies a deep-research Markdown file (~40 source links, AI adoption in medium-sized enterprises, e.g. Perplexity export); Karpathy-pattern ingestion creates `raw/` entries and interlinked `wiki/` pages, potentially fanning out to a few hundred pages/connections, replacing the 2-page placeholder vault (B11).

## Priority Signal

Issue #4's own suggested loop ordering, confirmed by the user's framing:

1. Core broken interactions: search in default view (A1) + clickable Related/descriptions (B4).
2. Biggest visible polish per hour: full pill labels (B5), stats footer (B7), legend + start-anywhere panel (B3/B2).
3. Force-directed framing + focus mode (A2/A6).
4. Design-sense layer: hero (B1), fonts (A9), palette (B10).
5. Demo vault (B11) — prerequisite for the deployed page being impressive; user wants this as its own research+ingestion epic and will supply the deep-research MD input.
6. Remainder: A3 (with repo-public decision), A4, A5, A7, A8, B6, B8 (single tour), B9.

User decisions this cycle: single tour (not persona tours); descriptions from frontmatter with first-paragraph fallback; repo goes public after a history audit; demo vault ~40 ingested sources fanning out to potentially a few hundred wiki pages, as a separate epic fed by a user-provided Perplexity deep-research MD.

## Deferred Items

- Persona-based multi-tours ("I'm new here" / "I build things" / "I run a business")
- Arrow-key node-to-node keyboard graph traversal
- Automated research pipeline (deep-research input stays manual/user-provided)
- In-app raw-markdown reader
- Analytics on node/query/tour engagement
